    "body": "@gterzian I don't think we need to change the dispatch algorithm. We'd have a standalone \"has a listener\" or some such algorithm that takes an EventTarget and a type and that basically iterates over the event listeners of that EventTarget to see if there's any with that type. \r\n\r\nWe could then use that hook in the unload/prompt to unload to determine if there are any unload/beforeunload listeners for the document.\r\n\r\nOn the DOM side this is tracked by https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/453. If you want to work on that, that'd be great!",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
